{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538187-w20-rage-across-the-heavens","id":1538187,"title":"[W20] Rage Across The Heavens","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-06T19:59:28-07:00","id":1538187,"title":"[W20] Rage Across The Heavens","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> Some questions about Rage Across The Heavens and W20:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The book is compatible with W20 right?</li> <li>On page 126, there is a preface to the Zodical merits and flaws, stating that players &quot;<i>may purchase a maximum of seven points worth of Merits or take up to seven points of Flaws</i>&quot; is this because Merits and Flaws were a new mechanic at the time the book was written or some restriction intrinsic to the Zodical Merits/Flaws? So you can not take more than 7 on a W20 game?</li> <li>The <b>Mother\u2019s Insight </b>merit, has Wits related benefits and states &quot;<i>Additionally, in situations where three or more successes are required, you need one less to accomplish your task</i>&quot; Is this only for Wits rolls or all rolls?</li> <li>The Planetary Aspects section mentions that characters should possess either Planetary or Zodical merits/flaws, not both. Has this ruling been overridden on any further book?</li> <li>Isn't the <b>Mars Midsky</b> &quot;merit&quot; too expensive for being mainly a drawback? Is there any errata for it?</li> <li>General question on Frenzy, how do interact the rulings that set your Frenzy successes at a set number?<br /> For example, the <b>Mars Midsky</b> merit makes you frenzy with 2 successes, at Rank 5 you frenzy at 5+ successes,<b> Rite of the Silver Forge</b> makes you frenzy at 6 successes.<br /> I have used the ruling that Rank and Silver Forge are meant to increase the number of successes needed, not a fixed value (so Rite of the Silver Forge + Rank 5/6 still has a benefit) but would like to confirm.</li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 07-07-2024, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-08T14:42:59-07:00","id":1538256,"title":"","content":"The limit of 7 points in Merits/Flaws was in general, not just for Zodiacal ones, and wasn't new.<br /> <br /> Before W20, Merits and Flaws didn't appeared on the Core book of any line, just on supplements. So every book with Merits and Flaws within it had to explain the limit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-03T11:35:36-07:00","id":1539760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1538187-w20-rage-across-the-heavens?p=1538256#post1538256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The limit of 7 points in Merits/Flaws was in general, not just for Zodiacal ones, and wasn't new.<br /> <br /> Before W20, Merits and Flaws didn't appeared on the Core book of any line, just on supplements. So every book with Merits and Flaws within it had to explain the limit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, that helps. Anything to add to the other questions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T15:44:55-07:00","id":1539952,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11620_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11620\" data-vbnamecard=\"11620\">twig</a> yours are some of the voices that I would love to chip in this topic, given your extense experience and well argued posts.<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T16:09:28-07:00","id":1539955,"title":"","content":"I didn't read Rage Across the Heavens, so I can't say much more about it. It's as compatible with W20 as any Revised era book can be, which means it's up to the Storyteller, and I don't think there's any update on this material one way or the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-06T19:52:09-07:00","id":1539965,"title":"","content":"You may already know this, but the only errata you could ever expect from WW or its successors about anything is the Exalted 2e document. If it's not altered in another edition, you're on your own.<br /> <br /> With that in mind, I had some thoughts about the Gifts from years back, and they mostly involved the typical kind of rethinking that a lot of Gifts got into W20, with some planetary Gift flat out becoming just W20 Gifts under a different name - for instance, I believe there's a Ruatma Gift that has a long and circuitous way of reaping omens and such with its system. I took a cue from the Qualmi Gifts for that and turned it into that Gift that just gives a permanent +3 bump to your Enigmas dice pool. The nature of 2e Gifts is very hit and miss, so I recall doing that a fair bit.<br /> <br /> As for merits, Mars Midsky should frenzy at 3 successes, because it was copied over carelessly from 1e, when it only took 3 successes to frenzy, and its effect was to reduce the number of successes required to frenzy by 1. The Rokea should also technically be there, or even further above it, because to be quite frank for this tangent, sharks don't actually go fucking nuts more frequently than mammals. It's kind of like that incident where some dude saw piranhas strip a pork side or something in seconds; they had all been starved days prior to this, and W:tA being W:tA, people should know this as be ready to get acquainted with new, better-conducted wildlife research that flies in the face of their assumptions.<br /> <br /> (Turns burning gaze to the Suchid Breed description of the Mokole for a painful moment)<br /> <br /> Anyway. Mars Midsky still gives a pretty hefty bonus for when you're in a frenzy, which is almost on par with a Rank 5 White Howler Gift, so 5 freebies is probably fine as a cost even with one fewer success to frenzy.<br /> <br /> For Mother's Insight, it probably applies only to Wits-utilizing rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-07T19:42:51-07:00","id":1540029,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> thanks for the answers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}